<<~ ahu slot=`#/testability-scout-wave-1`>>

! Testability scout, wave 1 (codebase only)

Kilo-Scout: Lares (Tasked Spirit). Date 2026-10-31. Main checkout, read-only. Nothing in the repo changed; no mutation tool, suite, e2e or docker ran.
Anything I could not verify is marked ''(testimony)''.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/tl-dr`>>

!! TL;DR

# The 1.66:1 figure runs ''high'' against what I measure. Non-comment TS/MJS: tests 204,871 vs source 145,127 = ''1.41:1'' (1.46 with fixtures and shell witnesses). Raw lines: ''1.10:1''. Source carries 39% comment lines, tests 22%, so the raw view hides test weight and the comment-stripped view shows it. The weight sits in `lararium-node` (1.88), `lararium-web` (2.02), `lararium-tw5` (1.50) and `lararium-keyhive` (1.60). Node + mesh + tw5 hold 74% of all test LOC.
# The single biggest seam is one function: `prepareNodeBootOn` in `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:709-3546` runs ~2,840 lines (164 top-level closures/consts, 49 `let`s). Every claim about vessel boot enters through it, which is why tests boot whole vessels and stand setup in bulk.
# Test weight comes from setup repetition and breadth, not giant test files: 1,032 `mkdtemp` calls in 389 files, 2.1 test files per source file in node, 5,669 exports of which ~350 only tests touch (strict) and ~1,200 touch only their own file and tests.
# Mutation testing exists only as a hand catalog: 14 mutants for `lares-cli` (`packages/lares-cli/tests/laws/mutants.json`), run by `tools/law-mutants-witness.sh`. Stryker is not in the repo (no config, no dependency); canon records it activated no mutants against vitest 5. A mutation score cannot replace raw count today.
# The road (`stable-founding-road.mem:268, 849`) rules the test architecture re-cuts AFTER the founding. Items below sort into before (cheap, seam-opening, no re-cut), folded into the founding, or after. The "before" set needs the operator's explicit lift of that ruling.

<<~/ahu>>

