<<~ ahu slot=`#/where-the-test-weight-comes-from`>>

!! Where the test weight comes from

# ''Setup repetition.'' `mkdtemp` appears 1,032 times in 389 files across tests/tools; `lararium-node/tests` alone 598 in 233 files. Node has ONE shared setup file (`tests/support/scratch-custody-setup.ts`, 108 lines) and no shared temp-dir helper. Fixture helpers exist per domain in mesh and keyhive (`face-gate-fixture`, `kel-fixture`, `content-key-fixture`...). Same-named helpers redeclared across test files: `said` 12, `missing` 12, `sleep` 8, `meme` 7, `walk` 6 (git grep over function decls).
# ''Whole-vessel boots for unit-sized claims.'' Only 5 direct `openNodeVessel(` calls in tests, but 39 test files import `open-node-vessel` and 20 reference some vessel opener. Because the composer is one 2,840-line function, a claim about any closure (boot ordering, a gate, a sweep) reaches it only through the whole composition. 66 node suites sit in the serial `heavy` project (`packages/lararium-node/vitest.config.ts`) because they bind listeners, nested Workers or python holders; `maxWorkers: 4`. The e2e set (36 files in `tests/e2e`) carries `tools/e2e-shard-weights.json`: 35 files, 3,070 weighted seconds; top: nexus-two-root 330s, vessel-reboot 259s, hosted-walk 206s. Boot cost per `tests/vitest.config.ts` comment: "~30s incl. genesis".
# ''Test-only exports.'' No convention marks them (grep for `ForTest`, `test-only`, <code>&#64;internal</code>: 2 hits). By use graph (script `exp.mjs`, my scratchpad): 5,669 top-level exports in `packages/*/src`; ''350'' have no use in any other src file (barrels excluded), appear in tests, and no use in their own file beyond the declaration; ''1,198'' have no other-src use but appear in tests (own-file use allowed); 69 appear nowhere (dead). The 350 by package: mesh 215, node 62, tw5 27, browser 13, mempalace 11, keyhive 10, cli 8. The prior scout's 233 sits in the same order of magnitude ''(testimony: its method is unrecorded)''. Caveat: a regex scan cannot see consumption by `bin/`, `.mjs` tools, package.json `exports`, and name collisions inflate "used". Treat as a candidate list.
# ''Giant files.'' Test files are not the driver (p90 = 223 lines); the god-file is the production composer. Breadth drives weight: node 2.1 test files per source file, browser 1.8, mesh 1.3.
# ''Witness shell scripts.'' `ls tools/*witness*.sh` = 54 files (4,790 raw lines). Most are 5-20 line wrappers around an `.mjs` with its own `*.test.mjs` (e.g. `ahu-pair-parity-witness.sh`, 14 lines): they measure live canon, not duplicate suites. Heavy ones are overlap candidates: `contract-witness.sh` 715 lines (two-vessel handshake; `tests/e2e/nexus-two-root.test.ts` is the same family, ''overlap unverified, testimony''), `household-https-witness.sh` 350, `hearths-gate-witness.sh` 293, `genesis-parity-witness.sh` 293. `witness-all.sh` globs `tools/*witness*.sh` (a new one enrols itself); 9 are held out as docker/browser.
# ''Prose/regex reading tests.'' 62 test files read `src/` bytes; 67 read `.ts` text. The CLI census (`cli-test-laws.mem` #/the-census) counted for the CLI alone: 206 prose-coupled assertions, 196 mocks mirroring the implementation, 100 giant fixtures, 60 source-regex reads, 29 timing waits, 24 tests that cannot fail, 23 touching outside a scratch root. Other packages likely repeat the smell classes ''(testimony)''.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seams-modules-that-resist-small-tests`>>

!! Seams: modules that resist small tests

| Seam | Evidence | Refactor that lets a smaller test reach the claim |h
| `prepareNodeBootOn` mega-closure | open-node-vessel.ts:709-3546; 164 closure decls, 49 `let`; `composeNodeVesselOn` (:3557) is ~100 lines and thin | Cut into named stages with typed input/output records; each stage tests with a small fake. Same shape for `open-browser-vessel.ts` (1,963 raw lines). |
| `identityDir()` reads env alone | `tests/harness/with-lar-root.ts:1-35` header: no caller path; a test that forgets `LAR_ROOT` silently touches `~/.local/share/lares/identity`; `withLarRoot` mutates `process.env` and "NOT thread-safe against concurrent vessels" | Pass a homes record (identity/storage/seal) into the opener; `vesselCustodyHomes()` (`vault-carriers`) is the seed. Read `LAR_ROOT` once at the process edge. |
| Git global config leak | `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` appears in 4 files; set at `packages/lararium-node/tests/support/scratch-custody-setup.ts:~35` and pinned by `hermetic-git-global.test.ts`; the source shells `git config --global user.email` in `readLocalOperatorHint`. Only node's setup file sets it; mesh/tw5/cli/keyhive configs not checked for an equivalent ''(testimony)'' | Inject the operator hint as a dependency so units pass a literal; keep one test on the shell-out; lift the null-device env into a shared workspace `globalSetup`. |
| Module-level registries | 74 module Maps/Sets in 53 files; `tests/vitest.config.ts` header says suites depend on `isolate: true` because modules "hold process-global registries … no reset clears" | Registries built in a composition root and passed in; the `isolate` dependence then drops. |
| Fixed waits / poll loops | 44 `turn < N` poll-loop lines in 27 test files; 77 `setImmediate` in 44 files; 699 `sleep/waitFor/until` hits. `wiki-shore-draft-road.test.ts:463,466,633`: 400 turns x 5ms polls `ledger.landedOf(x)`. `LandedLedger` (`lararium-tw5/src/landed-ledger.ts`, 14 lines) is a bare Map with no event | `whenLanded(title, pred)` promise on the ledger (about 10 lines) removes the flake class. The road already names this ("fixed waits become events"). |
| Wall-clock ratios | `sensorium-consistency.scale.test.ts:100-119` already cured: counts operations, with a comment citing the 12.48-vs-12 flake. Model for the rest | Sweep other `performance.now`/`Date.now` assertions in tests; not counted yet. |
| Staged-unlock under load | owed.md: 3rd sighting 2026-10-28, 4th 2026-10-30: "staged vessel never unlocked (door rc 1) ... store did not acknowledge &lt;doc> at rest" | Expose a store-ack event on the unlock door and have `tests/harness/instance.ts` await it. owed.md says the same. |
| TW5 dropdown e2e | `packages/lararium-web/tests/e2e/shore-writes.e2e.test.ts:150-164`: `.tc-search-drop-down` visible-wait of 20s; owed.md: 3 sightings 10-30/31 | Ready signal from the served page after the worker settles; capture `browserConsole` + mirror DOM on failure (owed.md proposes the capture). The popup depends on a late TW5 worker event. |
| Built `dist/` dependence | `tools/vitest-dist-guard.mjs` globalSetup; config comment: nested-worker ESM import of an existing dist file reds `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` under FD pressure | A source loader for workers removes the dist dependence. Wave 2. |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/mutation-testing-as-it-stands`>>

!! Mutation testing as it stands

* ''Stryker: absent from the repo.'' `git ls-files | rg stryker` and `rg -il stryker` (outside node_modules) hit only `bags/.../cli-test-laws.mem` and a vendored `automerge-repo` package.json. Canon: "Stryker 10 runs against this suite's vitest 5 and activates no mutant at runtime: every score read the same, killing only mutants that act at load. The named catalog stands in until a runner activates them" (`cli-test-laws.mem` #/the-holes). The inPlace-revert incident rests on an ad hoc run ''(testimony)''.
* ''Catalog runner:'' `tools/law-mutants.mjs` (42 lines), `tools/law-mutants-witness.sh`, `packages/lares-cli/tests/laws/mutants.json` (''14 mutants''), `packages/lares-cli/vitest.law-mutants.config.ts`. It rewrites a source file in place, runs the named law files, restores in `finally` and on SIGINT/SIGTERM. The `*witness*.sh` name makes `witness-all.sh` glob it into the witness fleet and CI. It mutates the working tree (same in-place hazard class as Stryker); SIGKILL would leave a mutant behind ''(inferred, untested)''.
* ''fast-check:'' `fast-check 4.10.2` and <code>&#64;fast-check/vitest 0.5.0</code> in `packages/lares-cli/package.json` only; 5 law files use property APIs; 18 law modules, 2,922 lines in `tests/laws`; seed fixed in `tests/laws/fixed-seed.ts` (`LARES_FC_SEED` overrides). Laws L1-L16 listed in `cli-test-laws.mem` #/the-laws. Finds reported there: four faults on first generated runs (TOML scalar/table kinds, duplicate floor write, replace reaching inside a table) and a fifth from the readiness law.
* ''Retirement so far:'' 55 literal tests retired where a law covers the input; 3 files removed whole; 1,000 rows classed (581 seeds, 230 repeats, 189 controls, 15 orphans). That is the only demonstrated "prune what a stronger test covers" in the tree, done by hand with two cold readers.
* ''Assessment: can mutation score replace raw count?'' Not yet. (a) No runner works with vitest 5. (b) 14 hand-written mutants on 17.6k CLI lines measure laws, not the suite. (c) The law + seeds + control + named-mutants recipe works and is the template. A "prune tests that kill no unique mutant" rule needs per-test kill sets; Stryker's `coverageAnalysis: "perTest"` gives them in principle ''(testimony; wave 2)''. Scoring before the founding measures shapes that will change.

<<~/ahu>>

