<<~ ahu slot=`#/canon-constraints-that-bind-recommendations`>>

!! Canon constraints that bind recommendations

* `stable-founding-road.mem:268, 849`: the test architecture re-cuts after the founding (operator ruling, 2026-10-29); until then large batches and one heavy battery per batch; red-first commits stay. Named inputs: fixed waits become events (`owned-store` first), tw5 corpus scans share one measured budget, node's slowest files get profiled. The CLI re-cut is the pattern awaiting "more eyes".
* Rulings "Old shapes burn" and "Full models land early": no tolerant readers, no staged interims; a seam-opening refactor leaves no back-compat shim and no second shape.
* `working-procedures.mem` #/red-first: vector before cure (own commit), read the failure text, nonsense control, assert the setup took, dispatch-position match, cure and check both marks move, a red that clears with no edit names shared state. For a refactor: a characterization test lands before the cut, and its control stays red after.
* `mixed-model-swarm.mem` #/the-battery: CI + held-out give the verdict; local battery = `pnpm build`, red proofs, evergreen boundary, `witness-all.sh`, typecheck witness, touched packages' suites (mesh always) under scratch HOME/LAR_ROOT with `LAR_BAGS` unset, `node --test` on touched tools, ONE e2e file; one heavy battery at a time via `tools/battery.sh`. A lane touching `open-node-vessel.ts` inherits the node suite plus mesh.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ranked-findings`>>

!! Ranked findings (value / cost / order vs the founding refactor)

Cost: S = under a day for a lane, M = days, L = a train.

# ''Stage-cut `prepareNodeBootOn` (and `open-browser-vessel.ts`)'' into typed stages. Evidence above. Gain: stage-level tests replace vessel boots; the 66-suite serial heavy project can shrink over time. Cost L, risk high (the most-touched file). ''FOLD into the founding refactor'' (the N/W/H trains already reshape boot); write characterization tests for the boot sequence BEFORE.
# ''Shared `withScratchRoot()`/`scratchHomes()` helper + codemod'' (1,032 `mkdtemp` in 389 files). Gain: fewer lines per test; one place fixes tmpdir, HOME, LAR_ROOT, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL. Cost M, mechanical, no product change. ''BEFORE'', in the porch lane (matches the hermetic-test owed items). Pilot on 20 node files and measure the LOC drop before sweeping.
# ''Eventful seams for the four flake families'': `LandedLedger.whenLanded`, store-ack event on the unlock door, ready attribute plus failure artifacts for the TW5 dropdown, event instead of poll in the browser two-tab test. Cost S each; removes 14+ owed sightings. Matches the road's own "fixed waits become events". ''BEFORE''; red-first fits (force the late event to reproduce).
# ''Inject homes and operator hint instead of reading env.'' Removes `withLarRoot` env mutation, the git-global leak and the silent-real-home footgun. Cost M. ''FOLDED'' into the custody/home work of the road; land item 2 first so the later change touches one helper.
# ''Delete the 69 dead exports now; list the ~350 test-only candidates with a TS-compiler pass; move survivors behind a `…/testing` subpath export during the module re-cuts.'' Gain: smaller public surface, and a clear view of which functions are real contracts. Cost S (dead) then M. ''BEFORE for the dead set and the list, DURING the founding for the moves.''
# ''Extend the law pattern to a second package'' (generated inputs, seeds, control, named mutants). Candidates by smell: `tw5` wiki-shore vectors, `mesh` face-gate and content-key-holder (vector tables over 1,000 lines). Gain: the one demonstrated route that cut tests. Cost M per package. ''AFTER'' (the road assigns the re-cut there), with at most one pilot beside the founding since fast-check is installed in lares-cli only.
# ''A working mutation runner with vitest 5.'' Probe each Stryker release or extend the catalog per package; run in a worktree copy, never inPlace on a live checkout; per-package, `perTest` coverage. Cost M, mostly probe time. ''BEFORE as a probe, USED after the founding'' for pruning.
# ''Witness consolidation'': one manifest for the 5-20 line wrappers; decide overlap of the four 200-700 line witnesses vs `tests/e2e`. Small LOC gain (4.8k); gain is runtime. Cost S-M. ''AFTER''.
# ''Report the ratio as non-comment.'' Source carries 39% comment lines (237,782 raw vs 145,127 code), so the raw ratio understates test weight by 0.3. No cost.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/questions-for-wave-2`>>

!! Questions for wave 2 (internet)

# StrykerJS with vitest: which versions support vitest 5 (canon says Stryker 10 activates no mutants); `coverageAnalysis: "perTest"` behavior; `--incremental` file stability across refactors; running in a sandbox copy not inPlace; per-package `mutate` globs in a pnpm monorepo.
# Alternatives to Stryker for TypeScript (AST-based mutators, vitest-aware runners) that avoid the hand cost of the named catalog.
# Mutation-guided suite minimization (kill-set reduction): papers, tools, rates of redundant tests found, and the regression value pruning loses outside the mutation operators.
# Test-to-code ratio norms: published ratios for monorepos, crypto and distributed-systems code, TypeScript; property-heavy vs example-heavy; whether published figures strip comments.
# Vitest: per-project `isolate`, `pool: threads` vs `forks`, `--shard` and sharding by weight (versus our hand-kept `e2e-shard-weights.json`), `--changed`, memory limits; whether `isolate: false` is safe for suites that reset module registries; `vi.waitFor` vs event waits.
# Property-based testing to collapse example tests: fast-check model-based/commands testing for stateful stores (ledger, store-ack), Automerge/CRDT projects' practice, shrinking cost on large states.
# Hermetic-test practice: `node:test` `mock.timers`, injecting `fs`/`os.homedir`, avoiding `process.env` mutation under parallel suites.
# Composition-root testing: guidance for cutting a 2,000+ line async composer into stages with typed ports; how VS Code, Deno and TiddlyWiki upstream slice boot code for test.
# CI wall time: affected-only selection (Nx/Turborepo/vitest related), test impact analysis, remote result caching, flaky-test quarantine policy.
# Playwright flake practice: web-first assertions, trace-on-retry, browser caching keyed on version, console-capture artifacts.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/method-notes-and-limits`>>

!! Method notes and limits

* Counts use my own comment stripper (leading-line `//`, `/* */`, `*`); trailing comments and template-literal text count as code.
* The export scan is regex-based (top-level `export const|function|let|class|enum`); it skips `export {x}` lists, default exports, type exports and barrel `index.ts`; candidates only.
* I measured no suite runtime, read no CI logs, and read no live-lane worktree.
* plan.md:345 (POSIWID scout, 2026-10-31) carries "233 test-only exports; open-node-vessel.ts 3,770 lines": the second matches `wc -l` (3,771 raw lines in my count); the first ''(testimony)''.

<<~/ahu>>

